[{"name":"create_goal","description":"Create a goal only when explicitly requested by the user or system/developer instructions; do not infer goals from ordinary tasks.
Set token_budget only when an explicit token budget is requested. Fails if an unfinished goal exists; use update_goal only for status.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { create_goal(args: {
  // Required. The concrete objective to start pursuing. This starts a new active goal when no goal exists or replaces the current goal when it is complete.
  objective: string;
  // Positive token budget for the new goal. Omit unless explicitly requested.
  token_budget?: number;
}): Promise<unknown>; };
```"},{"name":"get_goal","description":"Get the current goal for this thread, including status, budgets, token and elapsed-time usage, and remaining token budget.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { get_goal(args: {}): Promise<unknown>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__status__status_set","description":"Publish where your work stands (replaces your previous status). When blocked, name what blocks you in blockedBy. See the server instructions for when and how.

status_set publishes where your work stands to a status card the human reads in Paseo instead of asking you "where are we?".
- Call it at the end of every turn that changed where things stand: started, finished or abandoned a step, got a result, became blocked, or started waiting on the human. Skip it for turns that changed nothing.
- Call it before your final reply, and add no closing line after it: a collapsed turn shows only its last message, so a short line after the status card would hide your answer.
- Each call replaces the whole status, so send every field every time, except goal.
- Write for someone who skipped the transcript: plain words, no internal jargon, no file paths unless they matter.
  - goal: one or two sentences on the whole job and its overall progress, so someone opening this workspace cold knows what it is for ("Ship the record-page redesign from #966 as 7 stacked PRs; 4 merged, QA fixes next"). Send it on your first call and again when the job or its overall progress changes; leaving it out keeps the last one.
  - title: a few words, at most 60 characters, naming what this chat is about ("Gift-card checkout"). Send it on your first call and again when the chat's subject changes.
  - tldr: one or two sentences. Where things stand right now.
  - now: what you are doing or waiting on this moment.
  - done: finished steps, each with its proof ("tests pass: 105/105", "PR #22 open, CI green"). Say "not committed" or "not pushed" when that is true.
  - next: what is left, in order. Mark what needs the human.
  - state: working, waiting_on_you, blocked or done. Use working while you, a heartbeat or a background job still own the next step; waiting_on_you when the human has to act; blocked only when nothing can move until another workspace or another person acts (a child workspace still running, a peer's code review), not for CI, builds, deploys or your own subagents, which are working; done once nothing is left for you or the human, so next is empty. Finished work that waits on the human to test, review or merge it is waiting_on_you, not done. When blocked, list what blocks you in blockedBy: {kind, ref, reason?} with kind pr (ref "owner/repo#N" or URL), agent (agent id), workspace (workspace id), person (a name) or other.
- Messages starting with [status] are the human asking for an update: call status_set.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__status__status_set(args: { blockedBy?: Array<{ kind: "pr" | "agent" | "workspace" | "person" | "other"; reason?: string; ref: string; }>; done?: Array<string>; goal?: string; next?: Array<string>; now?: string; state: "working" | "waiting_on_you" | "blocked" | "done"; title?: string; tldr: string; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"multi_agent_v1__close_agent","description":"Close an agent and any open descendants when they are no longer needed, and return the target agent's previous status before shutdown was requested. Completed agents remain open and count toward the concurrency limit until closed. Don't keep agents open for too long if they are not needed anymore.

Tools for spawning and managing sub-agents.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { multi_agent_v1__close_agent(args: {
  // Agent id to close (from spawn_agent).
  target: string;
}): Promise<{
  // The agent status observed before shutdown was requested.
  previous_status: ("pending_init" | "running" | "interrupted" | "shutdown" | "not_found" | { completed: string | null; } | { errored: string; });
}>; };
```"},{"name":"multi_agent_v1__resume_agent","description":"Resume a previously closed agent by id so it can receive send_input and wait_agent calls.

Tools for spawning and managing sub-agents.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { multi_agent_v1__resume_agent(args: {
  // Agent id to resume.
  id: string;
}): Promise<{ status: "pending_init" | "running" | "interrupted" | "shutdown" | "not_found" | { completed: string | null; } | { errored: string; }; }>; };
```"},{"name":"multi_agent_v1__wait_agent","description":"Wait for agents to reach a final status. Completed statuses may include the agent's final message. Returns empty status when timed out. Once the agent reaches a final status, a notification message will be received containing the same completed status.

Tools for spawning and managing sub-agents.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { multi_agent_v1__wait_agent(args: {
  // Agent ids to wait on. Pass multiple ids to wait for whichever finishes first.
  targets: Array<string>;
  // Timeout in milliseconds. Defaults to 30000, min 10000, max 3600000. Prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.
  timeout_ms?: number;
}): Promise<{
  // Final statuses keyed by agent id.
  status: { [key: string]: "pending_init" | "running" | "interrupted" | "shutdown" | "not_found" | { completed: string | null; } | { errored: string; }; };
  // Whether the wait call returned due to timeout before any agent reached a final status.
  timed_out: boolean;
